<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<opml version="2.0">
<head><title>Business Model and Operations</title></head>
<body>
<outline text="Business Model and Operations">
<outline text="The program">
<outline text="Alpha Hours delivers the full Alpha academic day, after school, in two-hour sittings. Both subjects (Math and Reading/Writing) every sitting, mandatory, no single-subject option. Sittings are mixed K-8 because the platform individualizes every child's work. A family gets four hours a week: two weekday evenings of two hours each, or one four-hour Saturday block, morning or afternoon.">
</outline>
<outline text="The software (Timeback) delivers instruction and adapts to each child; guides manage focus, effort, and motivation, and do not teach.">
</outline>
</outline>
<outline text="Schedule and tracks">
<outline text="Weekday track: Monday and Wednesday, or Tuesday and Thursday, 5:00 to 7:00 pm. A student does not come all four weekday nights.">
</outline>
<outline text="Weekday setup: 4:45 to 5:00 pm (guides prepare, devices ready).">
</outline>
<outline text="Weekday block: 5:00 to 7:00 pm.">
</outline>
<outline text="Weekday dismissal and reset: 7:00 to 7:15 pm.">
</outline>
<outline text="Saturday setup: 8:45 to 9:00 am.">
</outline>
<outline text="Saturday AM block: 9:00 am to 1:00 pm.">
</outline>
<outline text="Saturday transition: 1:00 to 2:00 pm (staggered pickup and drop-off; no lunch served).">
</outline>
<outline text="Saturday PM block: 2:00 to 6:00 pm.">
</outline>
<outline text="Saturday reset: 6:00 to 6:15 pm.">
</outline>
<outline text="Every campus runs four cohorts a week: Monday/Wednesday, Tuesday/Thursday, Saturday morning, and Saturday afternoon. The same room and the same guide team serve all four, and every cohort gets the same four weekly hours.">
</outline>
</outline>
<outline text="Capacity">
<outline text="Room capacity is the seats filled at one time, set per campus.">
</outline>
<outline text="Enrolled students per campus is four times the room capacity: two weekday tracks plus two Saturday blocks. A 100-seat room fills to 400 enrolled students.">
</outline>
<outline text="The operating goal is to fill every cohort to capacity.">
</outline>
</outline>
<outline text="Enrollment">
<outline text="Five sessions a year, each about seven weeks (about 35 program weeks).">
</outline>
<outline text="Families sign up one session at a time, choosing a two-night track, with a one-session minimum. They re-enroll session to session.">
</outline>
<outline text="One session at a time lowers the barrier to trying Alpha and cycles far more distinct families through each seat than an annual plan.">
</outline>
</outline>
<outline text="Pricing">
<outline text="Session price: $4,500 premium markets, $3,500 standard markets. Full year (five sessions): $22,500 premium, $17,500 standard.">
</outline>
<outline text="Four to five times the priciest mainstream after-school competitor (about $875 for seven weeks). Roughly a third (30 to 40 percent) of full Alpha tuition for the year.">
</outline>
</outline>
<outline text="Real estate">
<outline text="The building is a sunk cost Alpha already carries, whether it owns the campus or leases it, with after-hours access either way. Evening and Saturday use adds only marginal cost.">
</outline>
<outline text="Marginal cost is $150 to $250 per weekday evening, about $400 per Saturday (custodial, HVAC and lighting, security). Because the host is an Alpha campus, the facility fee is largely intracompany.">
</outline>
</outline>
<outline text="Team">
<outline text="Head of Alpha Hours (Nancy Wisniewski Torvund): $400,000. Owns strategy, pricing, national rollout, campus relationships, conversion targets, and the full P&amp;L.">
</outline>
<outline text="Operations and Admin Manager: $110,000 to $130,000. Enrollment, billing, host-campus contracts, compliance, insurance, payroll, reporting.">
</outline>
<outline text="Campus Coordinator: $75,000 to $95,000. Launches sites, trains guides, runs quality, owns the parent experience. One, then more as sites grow.">
</outline>
<outline text="Site guides: $22 to $45 per hour by metro. Dedicated to Alpha Hours; about 20 staff-hours a week across four evenings and Saturday. Can also cover Alpha campus afternoon shifts for a blended full-time role of $50,000 to $85,000.">
</outline>
<outline text="Site lead / lead guide: $30 to $55 per hour. Runs the evening, owns dismissal safety.">
</outline>
<outline text="Staffing: about 1 guide per 10 students, two-adult minimum, extra attention to the youngest. Guides scale with the room, not the cohort count, so the same team serves all four cohorts.">
</outline>
</outline>
<outline text="Compliance">
<outline text="Design and market as academic instruction, not childcare, to qualify for state exemptions. Avoid meals where they trigger licensing (Florida especially). Sign a formal host-campus facility-use agreement. Get a written exemption determination per state before opening.">
</outline>
<outline text="Every block is a curriculum-driven instructional period; the Saturday four-hour block is structured as two two-hour instructional periods with a supervised break, and no lunch is served. Flag the Saturday format specifically in each state's written exemption request.">
</outline>
<outline text="Background checks on every hire: fingerprint criminal check, national sex offender registry, state child-abuse registry. Two adults on site at all times.">
</outline>
<outline text="Insurance: general liability, professional liability, workers' compensation, and sexual abuse and molestation coverage (excluded from most general liability policies, must be added).">
</outline>
</outline>
</outline>
</body>
</opml>
